Verify local controller prerequisites without installing or changing state. Omit --context for the host baseline; only an explicit nonempty --context adds that context's own target tools, the native closures its controller stage selects (the libvirt client, the hypervisor and the installer-media tooling) and its host binding.

Usage:
  bootwright preflight controller [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright preflight controller --context lab

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select explicit Environment requirements (default: baseline)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
